        {
          "case": "iff-forward",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Example of Worked example B01 — exact finite dynamics and its first coefficient: Use the two-level matrix model of [[thm-qft-example-finite-dyson-unitarity]] with $H=g_E\\sigma_x$, where $g_E>0$ is in joules. At $$t_1=\\frac{\\pi\\hbar}{2g_E}>0,$$ the exact off-diagonal matrix-element square is $1$, while its first-order squared coefficient is $\\pi^2/4>1$. At $t_2=\\pi\\hbar/g_E$, the exact survival matrix-element square is $1$, whereas $e^{-\\Gamma t_2}<1$ for every positive rate $\\Gamma$ in $\\mathrm{s}^{-1}$. These are finite-matrix identities. A later Born-rule interpretation may assign the exact square a probability; the mathematics here assigns no probability to an amplitude. The forward iff axis adds no separately stated converse hypothesis here; the recorded claim is the displayed construction, identity, implication or scope qualification, not a characterization by a new necessary-and-sufficient condition."
        },
